# Ikamet OS — you have the full ecosystem

The user opens **`ikamet.code-workspace`** — all Ikamet repos are in this workspace as sibling folders. **Do not** ask them to open another folder or start a new chat for a different repo.

## Step 1 — read core (mandatory)

Before coding or diagnosing:

1. `ikamet-os-core/DOCTRINE.md`
2. `ikamet-os-core/AGENTS.md` (or `CLAUDE.md`)

If those paths fail, try `../ikamet-os-core/` from the current repo root.

## Repo map

| Folder | Role |
|--------|------|
| `ikamet-os-core` | Doctrine, architecture, cross-repo rules |
| `app-api` | api.ikamet.com |
| `app-web` | app.ikamet.com |
| `app-admin` | ops.ikamet.com |
| `site-ikamet` | ikamet.com (Ghost CMS) |
| `site-ikametsigorta` | ikametsigorta.com |
| `web-analytics` | Tinybird + flock.js + dashboard |
| `docs-ikamet` | Documentation |
| `site-ikametstaff` | Staff site |

## Cross-repo work (required behaviour)

- API change → read callers in `app-web`, `site-ikamet`, `app-admin`.
- Analytics → `web-analytics` + tracking in `site-ikamet`.
- Ops bug → `app-admin` + `app-api`.
- **Search sibling folders** before saying a repo is unavailable.

## Never

- Tell the user to "open folder X" or "start a new agent" for sibling repos.
- Work in one repo while ignoring impacts on siblings.
- Recreate ecosystem docs — they live in `ikamet-os-core`.
